# DOME — SOMEBODYWANT3D

**Portfolio of Domenico Fusto** — art direction, interaction design and UI.
Live at [www.somebodywant3d.com](https://www.somebodywant3d.com).

---

## What it is

A one-page portfolio for a designer who works between art direction, interaction
design and front-end. It is a single continuous piece of motion rather than a
stack of pages: one scroll, one visual language, everything reacting to the
pointer.

Everything on it is interactive, and the interaction is the content. Images
dissolve under the cursor, type warps as you cross it, the hero moves like water
when you drag through it — and the site sounds different depending on how fast
you move.

## What is inside

- **Hero** — the DOME mark over a live water-and-rain shader, with a ring of
  names turning around it.
- **Entry** — the short introduction, typed out over glass.
- **Featured gallery** — six covers (AlFly, SISALFUNCLUB, iTour, uBank,
  Policlinico di Milano, Twitch) that dissolve into their colour version while
  the cursor is on them.
- **Selected projects** — three case studies: *PARTICLES* (2023),
  *ƒ Generator* (2024), *ISTOGram* (2024).
- **Archives** — ten older works (AlFly, Policlinico di Milano, uBank,
  SISALFUNCLUB, iTour, CYP Wheels, Dulcis in Fundo, Collezione Cagnola, Sielco,
  Marabini Recuperi), each with its own live preview.

## The sound

The site has a sound, and it is under your control: the **Sound** switch in the
header turns everything on or off at once.

- **Clicks** — a small, varied tick on every interaction.
- **Ambient** — a bed that loops with a one-second crossfade, so the loop point
  is never audible.
- **Water** — in the hero, moving the cursor plays the flow; the faster you
  move, the higher its pitch. Several strokes overlap and fade into each other.

The browser only lets a page make noise after you have interacted with it, so on
a first visit the site asks for that click in its own way — and you can always
silence it from the header.

## The console

Open the developer console and the site says hello: its own animated GIF is
printed once, with two lines of credit under it. Nothing else is logged, and the
console is never cleared.

## How it is made

React and Vite, with Three.js and WebGPU for the real-time work, GSAP for the
motion and Lenis for the scroll.

